        {
          "resource_id": "monster_action",
          "stats": {
            "action_name": {
              "value": "Dance of Ruin"
            },
            "action_description": {
              "value": "(divine, electricity, evocation, manipulate, move)\n\nThe vrock dances in flight and chants to create a ruinous explosion of electricity. If more vrocks within 30 feet want to join the dance, the vrock can delay the dance to wait for more vrocks; in that case, the effect occurs after the last vrock uses Dance of Ruin or one of the vrocks chooses to complete that round of the dance. Each non-demon creature in a 20-foot emanation from any of the dancing vrocks takes 2d12 electricity damage (28 basic Reflex save). For each additional vrock that joins the dance, the damage increases by 1d12 and the save DC increases by 1 (to a maximum of four vrocks dealing 5d12 damage with a 31 save). The vrocks can continue dancing by using Dance of Ruin each round, for up to 3 rounds in total. The emanation's size increases by 20 feet each round, and the damage increases by 1d12 per vrock each round."
            },
            "action_type": {
              "value": "none"
            },
            "action_cost": {
              "value": "three_actions"
